ut handler fires at 600s while the delegate buffer's\npipeline is STILL STREAMING (live sub-agents making requests).\nCurrent behavior: mark completed, gptel-abort the live request,\narm a 3s kill-buffer timer, callback the parent. The orphaned\nsub-agents keep running; their completion hooks, re-prompt timers\n(1s), and buffer-kill timers (3s/5s) race the abort/kill path.\nA timer or curl sentinel hitting a dead/nil buffer raises\nwrong-type-argument stringp nil -- the crash that killed the cycle.\n\n## Design decision: DRAIN, not abort\n\nThe task file lists two options: (a) extend the timeout once with\na warning, or (b) drain -- wait for sub-requests to finish, then\ncomplete with the partial result. Chosen: DRAIN, with a hard\nceiling. Reasons:\n\n- A pipeline that is still streaming is doing REAL WORK. Aborting\n  it destroys the sub-agents' output (the parent gets a timeout\n  message; the work is lost). Draining preserves it.\n- Extending \"once with a warning\" re-arms the same race at the new\n  deadline if the pipeline is still live then. Drain-with-ceiling\n  is the same idea but honest about the loop: keep draining while\n  live, up to a ceiling, then hard-stop.\n- The ceiling bounds the worst case: the parent's own delegate\n  timeout was already 600s; the drain adds at most\n  iar-delegate-drain-grace (default 300s) more. Total worst case\n  900s per delegate -- still far below the cycle watchdog's\n  1800s idle threshold (iar-agent-cycle.el resets idle on any\n  active request, and drained sub-requests ARE active requests,\n  so the cycle watchdog never sees a stall during a drain).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n1. New helper `iar--delegate-live-subrequests-p (buf)`:\n   Returns non-nil if gptel--request-alist has any entry whose\n   FSM :buffer is BUF (the delegate's own live curl request) --\n   i.e. the delegate is actively streaming. This mirrors the\n   lookup pattern gptel-abort itself uses (cl-find-if over\n   gptel--request-alist, comparing (gptel-fsm-info fsm) :buffer\n   to buf). A delegate with NO live request is between turns\n\n[t+04:11/60:00 c49/300]"},{"role":"assistant","conte...[+1853 chars]
