et-check\n  detector comparing go2rtc producer audio-bytes delta (flowing) vs\n  newest recorder segment n_samples (zero) -- flags the class within\n  ~10min instead of 30h. Will build next cycle unless you object.","filepath":"/root/personalization/relay/open/20260915-aria-0072-ext5-audio-dead-recordings-since-0027z-same-producer-session-class.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:52:24] Success: File written to '/root/personalization/relay/open/20260915-aria-0072-ext5-audio-dead-recordings-since-0027z-same-producer-session-class.md'\n[t+16:50/60:00 c170/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ubphoeqy","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"[2026-09-15 04:55:30] cycle: c353 -- EXT5 AUDIO DEATH MECHANISM FOUND. Pulse all green (services, tripwire, heartbeat, disk 30%, twin FAIL=0, census 0 true 429s, empty-end frozen 14). Fleet-check FAIL=1 -> root-caused: ext5 (.105) recorder writes video-only segments since 00:27:05Z (last audio 00/26.52.mp4). Camera healthy (uptime continuous, RSSI flat -53, mic enabled, rebooted 05:00:40Z Sep 14 per cron). go2rtc producer receives+forwards audio NOW (~4144 B/s 12s delta); restream decode carries 161k samples/10s. Recorder proc (started 21:50:43Z) survived; its audio track died. Producer read-timeouts 00:26:48+00:27:04Z coincide with death. Ext2 fine-scan corrected: .102 audio died 18:33:47Z Sep 14 (not 00:03Z Sep 15 -- 30h notice lag), no logged reconnect at death second (trigger not always visible). Class: recorder audio track death; heal = producer replacement (ext2 healed via 02:00Z reboot). Falsifier armed: .105 reboots 05:00Z -> expect audio back ~05:01Z. Relay 0072 filed. Mechanism doc: knowledge/aria/ext5-audio-death-mechanism-2026-09-15.md. 0915e arp logger alive (proc 3460747, output file 87.5KB, mtime 01:35 local -- boot-window read queued for 06:13Z expiry).","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:52:27]