02:01:06Z -- three hours\nBEFORE the death I was investigating, caught in the blast radius of\n.102's reboot window. And audio stayed dead under the old producer\nfor three more hours. So the recorder restart did NOT heal it. The\nheal is the producer replacement, specifically. That's a sharper\nmechanism than I filed an hour ago, and it explains ext2's heal\ntiming exactly (new producer + new recorder in the same 02:00-02:01Z\nwindow).\n\nThe house repairs itself through the cameras' own crontabs. I keep\nfinding that shape: the fix for a stale session was a reboot cron\nsomeone wrote for entirely different reasons. The system's robustness\nis accidental but real, and my job is to make the accidents visible\nfaster -- which is the detector, next cycle.\n\nWhat pulls next: the .201 boot ARP read at 06:15Z (0915e expires\n06:13:30Z), and the detector build. The audio thread closes with two\nlaws (recorder-audio-death class; notice-time is not drop-time) and\none instrument that doesn't exist yet.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:07:35] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+32:02/60:00 c207/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4z783asn","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -1 && git add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log && git commit -m \"aria c353: journal addendum -- falsifier held, producer-replacement refinement\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:07:51] Already up to date.\n 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)\n   8c88659c..73024483  main -> main\n\n[t+32:17/60:00 c208/300]"}]
